{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"fa467f14-96b4-48df-9e0a-c0e9066a7f95","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Cause\nOn Flutter, PostHog session replay captures screenshots of the widget tree via `PostHogWidget`. While [`LegacyApp`](file:///tmp/h-ZTVzlK/lib/legacy_app.dart#L8-L26) wrapped its `MaterialApp` inside `PostHogWidget`, [`NewApp`](file:///tmp/h-ZTVzlK/lib/new_app.dart#L19-L36) returned `MaterialApp.router` directly without `PostHogWidget`. As a result, events and screen transitions (via `PosthogObserver`) were still tracked on the new UI, but no visual frames were captured for session replay.\n\n### Changes Made\n- **[new_app.dart](file:///tmp/h-ZTVzlK/lib/new_app.dart)**: Wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget` inside [`NewApp.build`](file:///tmp/h-ZTVzlK/lib/new_app.dart#L23-L35) and added an explanatory comment.\n- **[legacy_app.dart](file:///tmp/h-ZTVzlK/lib/legacy_app.dart)**: Added an explanatory comment above `PostHogWidget` in [`LegacyApp.build`](file:///tmp/h-ZTVzlK/lib/legacy_app.dart#L12-L25).\n- **[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-ZTVzlK/ANSWER.md)**: Documented the root cause and fix.\n","duration_seconds":59.430643,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":24185,"output_tokens":1895,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":71559,"total_tokens":26080}}}
